 This is a straightforward problem involving vector operations. To find \(\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -5 \end{pmatrix} - 4 \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}\), we first multiply each component of the vector \(\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}\) by 4, and then subtract the resulting vector from \(\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -5 \end{pmatrix}\). \[
4 \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 4 \cdot -1 \\ 4 \cdot 7 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -4 \\ 28 \end{pmatrix}
\] Now we subtract this vector from \(\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -5 \end{pmatrix}\): \[
\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -5 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} -4 \\ 28 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 - (-4) \\ -5 - 28 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 + 4 \\ -5 - 28 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ -33 \end{pmatrix}
